  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manoj Kumar vs The State Of Bihar on 8 December, 2020 Author: Prabhat Kumar Singh Bench: Prabhat Kumar Singh In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.24554 of 2020 Arising Out of Ps. Case No.-2 Year-2013 Thana- Government Official C District- Gaya ====================================================== Manoj Kumar, Son of Ramchandra Prasad, Resident of Village - K.P. Lane, Near Mahadev mandir, P.S.- Kotwali, Distt.- Gaya. ... ... Pe Versus The State of Bihar ... ... Opposite Party/s ====================================================== Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Sudha Chandra, Advocate For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Uday Chandra Pd., A.P.P. ====================================================== Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Prabhat Kumar Singh Oral Order",
    "facts": "Petitioner apprehends arrest in a case registered for the offence punishable under Section 26(i)(ii) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, which is made punishable under Section 59(iii) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. As per the prosecution case, a sample of Arahar Dal was taken by the informant which was sent for analysis to Food and Drug Laboratory, Agamkuan and subsequently, the same was found to be of sub-standard, as a result of which this complaint case was filed in the Court of Special Judge, Gaya on 23.11.2012. On the basis of the aforesaid complaint, Complaint Case No. 02 of 2013 was registered on 05.01.2013 in which Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.24554 of 2020(4) dt.08-12-2020 cognizance has been taken on 05.02.2013.",
    "arguments": "It is submitted on behalf of the petitioner that from bare perusal of the complaint, it is apparent that there is no victim and no one has sustained any injury. No mandatory requirements of law with regard to sampling has been complied with. Petitioner was never given any notice and behind the back, the so called report was obtained. It is further submitted that, though, the cognizance has been taken on 05.02.2013 but summons was issued up to 30.05.2015 and without there being any service Manoj Kumar vs The State Of Bihar on 8 December, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/79989145/ 1 report, on 07.09.2015 bailable warrant was issued and without requisition of the same, non-bailable warrant was issued by the Court below on 12.01.2016 and the same was issued on 17.07.2019 i.e., only when petitioner has came to know about the institution of criminal proceedings against him . However, learned A.P.P. for State vehemently opposed the prayer for bail and submitted that there is allegation of selling of sub-standard Arahar Dal which does not confirm to the prescribed standard quality as laid down under the FSS Regulation, 2011.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted on behalf of the petitioner that from bare perusal of the complaint, it is apparent that there is no victim and no one has sustained any injury. No mandatory requirements of law with regard to sampling has been complied with. Petitioner was never given any notice and behind the back, the so called report was obtained. It is further submitted that, though, the cognizance has been taken on 05.02.2013 but summons was issued up to 30.05.2015 and without there being any service Manoj Kumar vs The State Of Bihar on 8 December, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/79989145/ 1 report, on 07.09.2015 bailable warrant was issued and without requisition of the same, non-bailable warrant was issued by the Court below on 12.01.2016 and the same was issued on 17.07.2019 i.e., only when petitioner has came to know about the institution of criminal proceedings against him . However, learned A.P.P. for State vehemently opposed the prayer for bail and submitted that there is allegation of selling of sub-standard Arahar Dal which does not confirm to the prescribed standard quality as laid down under the FSS Regulation, 2011.",
